{"term":"conservative","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:727a91f191ab959910","definition":"A person who favors maintenance of the status quo.","example":"During the late 1950s and throughout the 1960s, this commitment brought him into frequent critical confrontation with entrenched forms of conservative thinking (in academic areas from history and social science to the more abstract domains of ethical and political philosophy),[…]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cancervative","liberal conservative","national conservative","ultraconservative","neoconservative","one-nation conservative"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservative#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7705c4f9792bbbadb9","definition":"One who seeks to promote or preserve traditional values or institutions.","example":"If there’s a down side to the film, it’s that “Soros” probably doesn’t devote enough time to the way its subject has become a favorite bogeyman to conservatives that paint him as the guiding hand behind grassroots campaigns by those intent on discrediting them.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cancervative","liberal conservative","national conservative","ultraconservative","neoconservative","one-nation conservative"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservative#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b6461736c34ed52f68","definition":"One who seeks to promote traditions in a particular domain (e.g. a fiscal conservative or a social conservative).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Canada, US, especially","register":"Canada, US, especially","wordFamily":["cancervative","liberal conservative","n